From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: St0neWan9 <pawamaba@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:19:48 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: iCloud Keychain passkeys in the shell's
 WebAuthn dialog

Plan B130. iCloud Keychain passkeys (Apple's Passwords app and other
passkey provider apps) work once the app is signed with Apple's
com.apple.developer.web-browser.public-key-credential entitlement:

- Each request's window is the tab's NSWindow (the window of the
  WebContents' native view), through the previous patch's hook, so
  device/fido creates the iCloud Keychain discovery and macOS has a
  window for its sheet.
- The dialog offers iCloud Keychain: OACWebAuthnMechanismKindICloudKeychain
  for //chrome's generic "iCloud Keychain" method and
  OACWebAuthnMechanismKindPasskeyInICloudKeychain for one account's
  passkey (title: the account; subtitle: the app that holds it).
  Choosing one moves //chrome to kPlatformAuthenticator, which closes
  the dialog (withdrawn by the engine) while macOS shows its sheet.

Tests only: with --openarc-fake-icloud-keychain the bridge replaces
macOS's iCloud Keychain API (SetSystemInterfaceForTesting) with a
stand-in that lists two passkeys and answers create() and get() with
errors macOS gives, so the engine conformance test runs the path
without the entitlement. Chromium's own fake is testonly in GN; this one
is installed only with the switch, and nothing in it runs otherwise.
